The estimated value of $\gamma=1.005$, i.e.\ the US economy has experienced a
$0.5\%$ quarterly growth rate since 1960. Variable \textsf{ln\_gap}\ denotes
the detrended output. However, the empirical mean of the output is (still)
different from 0.

\begin{enumerate}
\item[c] Finally, we remove the empirical mean (which can be interpreted as
the steady state of the model):
\end{enumerate}

%

%TCIMACRO{\TeXButton{Minted}{\vspace{1ex}
%\begin{minted}[bgcolor=mygray,breaklines,linenos]{matlab}
