\vspace{1ex}
\begin{minted}[bgcolor=mygray,breaklines,linenos]{matlab}
figure;
plot(T,ln_y,T,trend_y)
title('Real GDP 1940-now')
figure;
plot(T,y)
title('Real GDP variations around the trend')
\end{minted}
\vspace{1ex}%
%EndExpansion


And save the transformed series of output into a matrix file, called
\textsf{mydata.mat}, which will be read by Dynare right after for the fit exercise.%

